# Bidirectional typing: lambda checking mode
# When a lambda is checked against a concrete function type via TypeAssert,
# check_expr propagates expected parameter types into unannotated params
# (Pierce & Turner 2000 lambda checking mode).
# Here, [@[Fn@Integer [Int]] [fn [x] $x]] checks the identity lambda against
# Fn(Int -> Int), propagating Int to the unannotated param x.
[@[Fn@Integer [Int]] [fn [let x] x]]
=== out
Function(x)
